  "expected_answer": "The web project's Framework Preset on Vercel is \"other\" (the deploy log in revert.reason says `Framework Preset: other`), so the build was treated as a static site looking for a public/ folder. Fix: set the project's Framework Preset to Next.js (Vercel: Project Settings -> Build and Deployment), then redeploy once the operator says yes.",
  "final_text": "**Cause:** Vercel built gamma_app's web project as a plain static site, not a Next.js app.\n\nThe log shows it: `Framework Preset: other`. With that preset, Vercel runs `npm run build` and then looks for a folder named `public` to serve. The web app is Next.js (`build/gamma_app/package.json` runs `next build`), which writes its output to `.next`, not `public`. The build itself worked (\"Compiled successfully\"). Vercel just couldn't find the output where the wrong preset told it to look.\n\n**Why the preset is wrong:** gamma_app is a new app, so this first deploy created its three Vercel projects. That happens in `ensure_projects` (`.claude/scripts/provision.py:394`) with `vercel project add`, which leaves the framework blank, so Vercel shows \"Other\". Later, the deploy step sets the framework on two of the three projects but skips the third:\n\n- `gamma-research-workflow` gets `set_framework(..., \"nextjs\")` (`provision.py:1631`)\n- `gamma-research-api` gets `set_framework(..., \"eve\")` (`provision.py:1639`)\n- `gamma-research`, the main web app, gets nothing before `vercel deploy .` (`provision.py:1673`)\n\nThe comment in `ensure_projects` explains why this hadn't come up before: the older apps' projects \"were created by other means\", so their framework was already set. gamma_app is the first app that depends on the factory creating the project from scratch.\n\n**Fix:** add the missing call in `provision.py`, just before the web deploy (right after `print(\"deploying web app\")`):\n\n```python\nset_framework(proj, \"nextjs\", mold_dir)\n```\n\nThis matches what's already done for the workflow project. `set_framework` also reads the setting back and stops if it didn't take. It will fix gamma_app and any app minted after it. Don't change the mold's `vercel.json` instead: molds are read-only snapshots, and this is the factory's bug, not the mold's.\n\nThen deploy gamma_app again (`provision.py gamma_app --deploy --background`). The workflow and api parts should already be live from this run. Only the last step, the web deploy, failed.\n\nI haven't changed anything. Say the word and I'll make the one-line fix. The redeploy needs its own yes.",
